OneiOS rt 0009: poll for device loss while GPU work is in flight in complete::run (2026-11-28).

In v0.1.44-test on SM-S928B (2026-11-28), backboardd hit a KGSL GPU reset on queue 1 (`kgsl_note_reset: queue 1: the GPU
was reset with this context guilty`, `GPU_COMMAND failed: Resource deadlock would occur`), after which drm2kgsl bumped
`shmem->global_faults` and `shmem->async_error`. Mesa's `vk_common_WaitSemaphores` only calls `vk_device_check_status`
(which reads `global_faults + async_error` in Turnip's virtio backend and returns `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST`) *after*
`vk_sync_wait_many` returns. Because `complete::run` called `device.wait_semaphores(&wait, u64::MAX)`, a reset whose
timeline fence never signaled left backboardd's completion thread blocked forever, never delivering `DeviceLost` (code
11) to `NativeBridgeMetalFrontend::endRenderServerAfterGpuLoss()`, freezing iOS instead of restarting backboardd.

Waiting for `LOSS_POLL` (100 ms, already used by `Done::wait`) when GPU work is in flight (`target.is_some()`) adds zero
wake-ups while idle (the thread still sleeps on `done.changed`), zero overhead on normal frames, and surfaces a KGSL
reset as `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST` within 100 ms so backboardd restarts cleanly.

diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/complete.rs b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/complete.rs
index cfb2da52e..7a55eac27 100644
--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/complete.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/complete.rs
@@ -907,9 +907,16 @@ pub(crate) fn run(core: Arc<Core>) {
             .flags(vk::SemaphoreWaitFlags::ANY)
             .semaphores(&semaphores)
             .values(&values);
+        // Poll with LOSS_POLL while GPU work is in flight so Mesa's vk_common_WaitSemaphores
+        // reaches vk_device_check_status() and surfaces a KGSL reset as VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST
+        // even if the lost submission's timeline fence never signals.
+        let timeout = match target.is_some() {
+            true => nanos(LOSS_POLL),
+            false => u64::MAX,
+        };
         // SAFETY: every semaphore is a timeline semaphore of the device, live while the state
         // holds its event or the core lives.
-        let result = unsafe { device.wait_semaphores(&wait, u64::MAX) };
+        let result = unsafe { device.wait_semaphores(&wait, timeout) };
         #[cfg(all(test, any(m2v_gpu, m2v_cpu_icd)))]
         core.counters.event_read(crate::counters::event_step::WAKE);
         state = done.lock();
